TEXT -48 -352 Left 3 ;#77 Op amp peak detector
TEXT -48 -280 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fn5kHhNRsz0
TEXT -48 -232 Left 2 ;The diode now sits inside the feedback loop. Feedback is taken from the capacitor, so the
TEXT -48 -192 Left 2 ;op amp raises its output by whatever the diode drops and C1 charges to the true peak.
TEXT 200 300 Left 2 ;Same hold network as circuit 02, so the
TEXT 200 332 Left 2 ;two can be compared directly. Alan does not
TEXT 200 364 Left 2 ;name the op amp; the LM358 is the part he
TEXT 200 396 Left 2 ;uses on the bench in video 75, that same week.
TEXT 200 460 Left 2 !.tran 0 40m 36m 100n
TEXT 200 508 Left 2 !.step param AMP list 1.5 0.25
TEXT 200 556 Left 2 !.meas tran VOUT_PK MAX V(vout)
TEXT 200 604 Left 2 !.meas tran VOUT_MIN MIN V(vout)
TEXT 200 652 Left 2 !.meas tran VIN_PK MAX V(vin)
TEXT 200 700 Left 2 ;LTspice runs a .step list in ascending order of value, not the order written,
TEXT 200 732 Left 2 ;so @1 on the plotted traces is the 0.25 amplitude, 0.5 V p-p, and @2 the 1.5, 3 V p-p.
